                           >Canterbury Cathedral Lit. A. 8 (68)</ref>.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">This is a bifolium, used as a wrapper for the
                     parish register (starting in 1552) of Elmstone, Kent. Elmstone Rectory was
                     listed as the current location in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                     Great Britain (1964). By 1985, the Rectory had been sold and was in lay hands.
                     The fragment could not be traced, as indicated in the supplement
                     (1987).</provenance>
